/-!
# Source-generated capacity-birth bearer exit

This file reuses the M14 UBI source stack but reindexes its employment and
independent-exit relations by the existing loss-allocation parent bearer.
The relation beneficiary is the existing `.t1` actor and the employment
controller is the existing `.t0` actor.  No actor type or identity registry is
introduced.

At each depth, the bearer-specific geometry consumes the existing periodic
payment, anomie phase, crossing, service compiler, and exact settlement.  Its
public carrier is additionally indexed by an already generated
`PeriodicActualServiceExitAt depth`; the payment occurrence and settlement in
the carrier are definitionally taken from that authority, not resupplied.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace ProcessGame
namespace Society
namespace M14SourceGeneratedContributionCapacityBirthBearerExit

noncomputable section

open ResponsibilityLifecycle LivingLawEvolution ConstructiveRoot
open Lifecycle Universal Relations Power Exchange Settlement Price Money UBI
open Renewal Capacity Space CrossingCost
open UBI.Capacity UBI.Capacity.SourceOwnedExitGeometryCompilerAt
open Lifecycle.Universal.FixedAdapter
open Settlement.SourceOwnedSettlementCompiler
open M3FiniteExchangeFixture M3ExchangeSettlementPriceRegression
open M8MoneyRootInstallationRegression M8PurchasingPowerStandingRegression
open M10OccurrenceCapacityProcessFixture
open M10OccurrenceCapacityDebitedRunFixture
open M11GeneratedSocialSpaceCrossingFixture
open M14UBIExitCapacityFixture
